WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.150
- [Narrator 1] Welcome to
Baarle-Hertog in Belgium.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.007
- [Narrator 2] No,
welcome to Baarle-Nassau

00:00:05.007 --> 00:00:06.302
in the Netherlands.

00:00:06.302 --> 00:00:07.335
- [Narrator 1] No, Belgium.

00:00:07.335 --> 00:00:08.168
- [Narrator 2] It's the Netherlands.

00:00:08.168 --> 00:00:09.001
- [Narrator 1] Belgium.

00:00:09.001 --> 00:00:10.350
- [Narrator 2] Netherlands.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.330
- [Female Narrator] OK,
everyone, please calm down.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.340
It's both.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.230
Welcome to the town with one of the most

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.663
intricate borders in the whole world.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.610
Baarle is a quiet, small-town
with not much going on,

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.830
until you look at these crosses.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.390
Yeah, that's an international border.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:35.370
And so it that, and so is that.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.000
Baarle is home to a living border puzzle.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.590
Instead of one border crossing,

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.570
there are dozens of them.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:44.860
And that's because the town
consists of 30 enclaves.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.490
There are 22 pieces of Belgium surrounded

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.950
by the Netherlands and 10
Dutch areas in Belgium.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.623
The border goes through
houses, shops, beer stores,

00:00:54.623 --> 00:00:58.450
and this means that there
are two of almost everything

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.112
for a population of under 10,000:

00:01:01.112 --> 00:01:03.130
Two postal services,

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.280
two churches,

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.900
two bus companies,

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.140
two legal drinking ages.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.160
There are even two mayo
toppings at this chicken shop.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.163
Yup, this one's Dutch,
and this one's Belgian.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.410
And there's two town halls.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.150
And, of course, a meeting
room with a borderline in it,

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.093
and two separate representatives.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.381
So how did the town get
into this messy situation?

00:01:27.381 --> 00:01:30.881
(speaks foreign language)

00:01:40.136 --> 00:01:41.810
- [Female Narrator] And
later on, this meant that the

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.480
Duke of Brabant possessed Belgian lands,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.364
and the Lord of Breda, Dutch lands.

00:01:47.364 --> 00:01:50.864
(speaks foreign language)

00:01:56.084 --> 00:01:59.625
(speaks foreign language)

00:01:59.625 --> 00:02:03.125
(speaks foreign language)

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:08.600
- [Female Narrator] Got it.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.160
So, head of tourism, Willem.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.420
How do you know where your house is

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.920
if the border goes through it?

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.990
- [Female Narrator] But,
what about front doors

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.960
that get chopped off by the border?

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.127
Like this one.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.483
- [Female Narrator] All right,

00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:51.690
but the international
commute, it must be tiring.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.023
Right, cafe manager, Willem?

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.360
- [Female Narrator] OK,
so my last question,

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.340
it has to be this:

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.267
Which town is best?

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:10.230
Baarle-Hertog, or Baarle-Nassau?

00:03:18.641 --> 00:03:20.724
(laughs)

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.180
- [Female Narrator] In
the end, it doesn't matter

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.060
which side of the border you choose.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.810
All in all, this is
just a great love story

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.370
between two countries.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.870
(speaks foreign language)

00:03:50.766 --> 00:03:53.849
(bicycle bell rings)

